upstream_path	decision	ported_path_or_none	check_only_first_line	note
extra/datasets/.gitignore	c-skip	none	NOT-RUN	asset row, not a .bend: 4 download-dir names (imagenet, imagenet_bak, mnist, open-images-v6TEST) and zero tinygrad API. Copied bytes here would only make git ignore directories this port never creates, because fetch is unported (helpers.bend:2815).
extra/datasets/__init__.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/__init__.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	NOT a thin fetch: IDX header offsets [0x10:]/[8:] (upstream:8-9) and the _load_disk_tensor assert idx == X.shape[0] (upstream:31). Hosts the shared D.Refused/D.refuse.
extra/datasets/fake_imagenet_from_mnist.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/fake_imagenet_from_mnist.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	Needs PIL Image.fromarray().save() (upstream:19) and multiprocessing.Pool(64) (upstream:36); module-level fetch_mnist() (upstream:9) returns Refused.
extra/datasets/imagenet.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/imagenet.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	No downloader at all; it is glob.glob over BASEDIR (upstream:22/29/34) under an MNISTMOCK fork (upstream:13) plus PIL resize/crop (upstream:41/52/75/84) and a 100-try rejection sampler (upstream:63).
extra/datasets/imagenet_download.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/imagenet_download.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	NOT class (c): the ILSVRC2012 tar is NOT credential-gated. Measured 2026-10-19 http=200 application/x-tar, 86900736 of 6744924160 bytes served anonymously. Blocked on tarfile, os.replace sort-then-rename (upstream:22-26) and fetch.
extra/datasets/kits19.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/kits19.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	Only file in the slice importing BOTH torch and tinygrad; resample3d uses mode="trilinear" for image and mode="nearest" for label (upstream:38-39), and pad_input's padding_val=-2.2 (upstream:108) must fall outside normal_intensity's clip (upstream:44).
extra/datasets/librispeech.py	c-skip	none	NOT-RUN	No tinygrad API at all (manifest MINIMAL_COPY, correct). Every computation is librosa.filters.mel/stft or soundfile.read (upstream:22/23/32/64); corpus is a MANUAL openslr.org/12 download plus an ffmpeg flac->wav pass (docstring upstream:8-16).
extra/datasets/openimages.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/openimages.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	Hinge is the join, not the table: get_image_list chains two isin (upstream:101-102) and export_to_coco numbers images by pd.factorize first-appearance (upstream:77). boto3 bucket is UNSIGNED (upstream:112), so also not credential-gated.
extra/datasets/preprocess_imagenet.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/preprocess_imagenet.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	UPSTREAM IS BROKEN, MEASURED: line 2 imports `iterate` from imagenet.py, which defines NO iterate (grep is empty; the only defs are kits19.py:73, squad.py:133, librispeech.py:67). ImportError at import time; never ran. Stub stops at line 2 and invents no iterate.
extra/datasets/sops.gz	c-skip	none	NOT-RUN	Binary asset, not source. gunzips to 4457 lines of captured `UOp(Ops.SINK,dtypes.void,...)` debug text, and NOTHING under extra/datasets/ references it.
extra/datasets/squad.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/squad.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	Half is pure and worth porting first: _check_is_max_context (upstream:43) and the stride-by-min(length,128) span loop (upstream:85). Blocked on fetch (upstream:11), transformers.BertTokenizer (upstream:4), and 0x202F NNBSP in the pretokenizer (upstream:22).
extra/datasets/wikipedia.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/wikipedia.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	Biggest and most portable in the slice: _is_punctuation is 4 ASCII ranges (upstream:39), _is_chinese_char is 8 codepoint ranges (upstream:44-51), _wordpiece_tokenize is greedy longest-match with ## (upstream:116-121). Blocked on unicodedata.category, and _is_control (upstream:30-31) must stay False for tab/newline/CR.
extra/datasets/wikipedia_download.py	b-needs-porting	tinybendygrad/extra/datasets/wikipedia_download.bend	ALL PROOFS CHECK	Not class (c): Drive ids are public and gdown is not a credentialed account. Real work is the unpack probe on "results4" (upstream:14) and the md5 verify_checksum (upstream:30-34); helpers.bend has getenv_str/getenv_int only, and the port has no md5 at all.